\n            continue\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n        sym = node['symbol']\\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) == 1:\\n            continue\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    removed_ids = removal_order\\n    retained_ids = sorted(retained)\\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_ids,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_ids\\n    }\"}\n\nCheck: we have newlines as \\\\n. In the string, we need to escape backslashes. In the above text, I have not escaped backslashes in the \\n in Python source (they appear as \\n). In the JSON string we are constructing, we need to write \\\\n. So in the actual response, we must write \\\\n for each newline. Also, need to escape any double quotes inside the string if any. There are none. So I'll write the string with \\\\n.\n\nAlso, the Python code uses single quotes, which are fine.\n\nNow, produce the final response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2198,"completion_tokens":6958,"total_tokens":9156,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2176},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":6522},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2176,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":22},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}